{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observed signal\nError sweep window 2026-09-01T11:58:00-07:00..2026-09-02T10:00:00-07:00 (2026-09-01T18:58:00Z..2026-09-02T17:00:00Z) found a Gerrit Verified Gate run that reached the final vote-cast step and then failed the GitHub Actions run because Gerrit rejected the review as targeting a closed change.\n\nRepresentative run: 33580445347 (Gerrit Verified Gate, workflow_dispatch, created 2026-09-02T01:42:29Z, head 024a6a2278134128be0c76c8d7c60e41b4ba817d). The `cast Verified` job had `WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION=success`, `VOTE_TYPE=success`, `GERRIT_CHANGE_NUMBER=2483`, `GERRIT_PATCHSET_NUMBER=7`, then failed with:\n\n`error: fatal: change is closed`\n`fatal: one or more reviews failed; review output above`\n\n## Root cause\nThe final Gerrit voting step treats Gerrit's `change is closed` response as a hard Actions failure even when the underlying gate work has already concluded and the patchset/change is no longer voteable. This creates red CI noise after a submit/close race rather than recording a benign superseded/closed disposition.\n\n## Plan\nReplace only the final `Cast Verified from the CI conclusion` step's opaque `gerrit-review-action` invocation with a trusted repo helper at `scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py`, checked out from the default branch by adding that path to the vote job's existing sparse-checkout list.\n\nThe helper will install the same SSH key/known_hosts material and invoke Gerrit's SSH review command for the `Verified` label, preserving the observed action-expanded command and run-URL message shape from run 33580445347 (`<STATUS>: <run URL>`). The run log for 33580445347 shows the action maps `success` to `LABELS=\"--label Verified=1\"`, `failure` to `LABELS=\"--label Verified=-1\"`, and `cancelled` to `LABELS=\"--label Verified=-1 --label Code-Review=-1\"`, then reaches `ssh ... gerrit review 2483,7 ...`. ADR 0023 defines the inbound path as SSH `gerrit review` setting `Verified +1` for success or `Verified -1` for failed/cancelled.\n\nResult classification and safety guards:\n\n- Map normalized vote-type domain to the same label tokens the action log shows: `success -> --label Verified=1`; `failure -> --label Verified=-1`; `cancelled -> --label Verified=-1 --label Code-Review=-1`.\n- Validate `CHANGE_NUMBER` and `PATCHSET_NUMBER` as positive decimal integers before invoking SSH, matching the existing cast/comment boundary.\n- Write the private key under `$HOME/.ssh`, chmod it `600`, write known_hosts, invoke `ssh -i <key> -p 29418 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes -- <user>@<server> ...`, and remove the private key in a `finally` path after the vote attempt.\n- If Gerrit output contains `fatal: change is closed`, print an Actions notice naming the change/patchset and exit 0 because the change has already moved to a terminal unvoteable state.\n- For every other nonzero SSH/Gerrit result, return the original nonzero exit code so real inability to vote an open change still fails closed.\n- Keep the start-of-run clear vote action unchanged; this bug is only about the final cast race after CI has completed.\n\nTest impact: rewrite the existing `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py` assertions that currently pin `gerrit-review-action` as the final cast step. In particular, replace `test_only_one_step_casts_a_vote` with a helper-focused assertion that the vote job has exactly one `Cast Verified from the CI conclusion` step, that this step runs `python3 scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py`, and that this final cast step no longer uses `gerrit-review-action`. Also update the normalized-vote and ordering assertions to locate the step by its name, and update the default-branch sparse-checkout assertion to include `scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Closed-change race: `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_closed_change_is_a_successful_noop` proves a Gerrit `fatal: change is closed` response exits 0 and emits a clear notice instead of reddening the run.\n- [ ] Real vote failures remain fail-closed: `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_other_vote_failures_still_fail` proves an unrelated SSH/Gerrit failure preserves its nonzero exit code and stderr.\n- [ ] Success vote shape is preserved: `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_success_vote_uses_the_verified_label_and_run_url` proves the helper sends `gerrit review <change>,<patchset>`, `--label Verified=1`, port 29418, and the run URL message.\n- [ ] Failure/cancelled vote shape is preserved: `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_failure_vote_uses_verified_minus_one tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_cancelled_vote_uses_verified_minus_one` proves `failure` sends `--label Verified=-1` and `cancelled` sends `--label Verified=-1 --label Code-Review=-1` with the matching status message.\n- [ ] SSH safety guards are preserved: `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_invalid_change_and_patchset_numbers_fail_before_ssh tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_private_key_is_chmod_600_and_removed_after_vote` proves bad change/patchset identifiers never reach SSH and the private key is chmodded and removed after use.\n- [ ] Workflow trust boundary is pinned: `pytest -q tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py` proves the vote job uses the default-branch helper, consumes the normalized vote type, posts triage detail only after the vote, and keeps the observability steps non-failing/comment-only.\n- [ ] Existing conclusion normalization and triage summarization still pass: `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion.py tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py`.\n- [ ] Repository gates pass for the changed paths: `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Testing\nRun the targeted workflow/script suite:\n\n`pytest -q tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion.py tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py`\n\nRun full code-quality gates:\n\n`make lint`\n`make typecheck`\n\nMutation check: temporarily reintroduce the defect by returning the Gerrit nonzero return code on `fatal: change is closed`, then run `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py::test_closed_change_is_a_successful_noop` inside `sandbox-exec`; it must fail RED, then restore the fix."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788373524672584584,"uuid":"6809bc43-4b15-4bf7-ae20-0230f03f7707"}